# Ask CAALM response bubbles: no gradient buttons

Inside an **assistant response bubble** (lifecycle cards, apply cards, pending-action footers, input forms rendered in the thread), do **not** use the teal-to-navy gradient pill.

## Forbidden in bubble content

- `btn-primary`, `primary-btn`, `shad-active`, `shad-submit-btn`
- Hand-rolled gradient fills that copy those classes

## Use instead — Cancel / Confirm (and similar)

Plain text actions. No icon required on these bubble footers.

```tsx
<button
  type="button"
  className="cursor-pointer text-xs font-medium text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-700 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50"
  onClick={onCancel}
  disabled={disabled}
>
  Cancel
</button>
<button
  type="button"
  className="cursor-pointer text-xs font-semibold text-[#0f5384] hover:underline disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50"
  onClick={onConfirm}
  disabled={disabled}
>
  Confirm
</button>
```

- Cancel: muted slate text
- Confirm / Start / Apply / Retry: brand `#0f5384` text, optional underline on hover
- Busy: keep the label; show a small spinner **only if needed**, never a gradient pill

## Out of scope (gradient OK)

- Sheet chrome outside the bubble: composer send, “New chat”, Focus chrome, sheet chips (`SHEET_CHIP_*`)

## When touching a bubble file

Search for `btn-primary`, `primary-btn`, `shad-active`, `shad-submit-btn` and remove every hit in bubble footers before finishing.
